{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AWS alarm sweep 2026-09-06 ~13:00 PDT (during incident-2ab6 follow-up): CloudWatch us-east-1 shows 0 alarms in ALARM, 0 INSUFFICIENT_DATA, all 30 OK; no state transitions since 2026-09-05 21:54 PDT. CPUCreditBalance for i-00880b2c7f13527c5 has recovered steadily since ~midnight: 29.8 (00:59 PDT) → 291.5 (11:59 PDT), still accruing; instance running as t4g.large. The acute zero-credit/billed-surplus condition described here has cleared. Note: there is currently NO CloudWatch alarm on CPUCreditBalance (the 30-alarm set covers disks/journals/services/gerrit checks but not credits), so a recurrence would again be invisible until symptomatic — consider adding one as part of this ticket's resolution. Plausible contributor to the Sep 5 credit exhaustion: the local-host memory incident (2ab6-bae5-8ca4-429c) drove heavy retry/clone traffic against Gerrit the same day."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788724767839039305,"uuid":"6949897b-b43a-4b76-8eb6-28a80c7f01f8"}